# BioVault Sentinel — Phase 1 execution policy

## Context
Read `docs/KT-phase1.md` for product/compliance context. Phase 1 = managed LTO-9 archival vault + Sentinel Dashboard (metadata online, tapes air-gapped).

## Stack
- Node 22 (ESM), TypeScript strict
- Express 5, MongoDB 7 (Mongoose), Redis + BullMQ
- React 19 + Vite + Tailwind 4
- Vitest (unit); Playwright optional Day 14

## Security (non-negotiable)
- No file content in MongoDB or API process memory beyond transient streams
- Client APIs must NOT expose tape barcode, rack, or slot — admin/technician only
- Passwords: bcrypt; sessions: httpOnly cookies; helmet + rate limits on API
- Retrieved files: `STAGING_PATH` only; time-limited signed download; purge after TTL/download
- Every mutating route → append `audit_events` (userId, IP, timestamp, action)

## SLA
- Retrieval `dueAt = createdAt + 15 minutes`
- Alert hook when job unassigned > 60 seconds (log/worker stub OK in MVP)

## Tape
- Implement `TapeLibraryAdapter`; MVP = `services/sentinel-api/src/tape/simulator.ts`
- Env `TAPE_ADAPTER=sim|mtx|scalar` for production swap
- Post-write: verify SHA-256 read-back before tape status `live`

## Monorepo boundaries
- Apps (`client-portal`, `admin-portal`) must NOT import each other or API internals
- Share only `@biovault/contracts` and `@biovault/common`
- API modules under `services/sentinel-api/src/modules/*` — avoid cross-module deep imports

## Certificates
- PDF + RSA-SHA256 or Ed25519; store PDF hash in `certificates` collection

## Out of scope
- DNA/crypto codec, cloud blob storage, file bytes on public API hosts
